9: 
10:     Input structure
11:     - A dominant background color and exactly one foreground color.
12:     - Four separated 8-connected foreground objects, each contained in a 3x3 bbox.
13: 
14:     Rule
15:     - Crop each object's 3x3 bbox, preserving its internal background holes.
16:     - Order the crops by their input positions: two upper sprites, then two lower sprites;
17:       within each pair, left before right.
18:     - Paste them into a 7x7 background canvas as 3x3 blocks with one blank row and one
19:       blank column between the blocks.
20: 
21:     Key insight
22:     - The input is an unpacked 2x2 sprite atlas; 8-connectivity keeps diagonal-only
23:       sprite pixels in the same object.
24:     """
25:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
26:     assert g.ndim == 2
27: 
